  "body": "I am reviewing a webpage that is using `<fieldset>` and `<legend>` to wrap related text information. The information is the results of a submitted form. \r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```\r\n<fieldset>\r\n  <legend>Contact details</legend>\r\n  <div><strong>Email address</strong></div>\r\n  <div>something123@getnada.com</div>\r\n  <div><strong>Mobile number</strong></div>\r\n  <div>0400000000</div>\r\n</fieldset>\r\n```\r\n\r\nAccording to the HTML specification this is perfectly valid as far as I can tell because the content model states: _Optionally a legend element, followed by flow content._\r\n\r\nIs this a valid way of grouping related (other content), and why is the fieldset / legend not restricted to related form controls only, considering there are other grouping elements for text? \r\n\r\n_'The fieldset element represents a set of form controls (or other content) grouped together, optionally with a caption.'_\r\n\r\nI'd like to understand the reasoning for including 'Other content' for the Fieldset element.",
